WEBVTT

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.360
<i>Hanamaru Kindergarten</i>

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:32.740
Good bye, sensei.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.300
Bye.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.490
Take care of yourselves over the summer break.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.230
Tsuchi seems happy even though he won't see me all summer.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:42.570
He's just happy about the long holiday.

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:43.830
Oh, I see.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.190
By the way, Tsuchi, will you be going home this summer?

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.170
No, I wasn't planning on it.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.640
Anzu, why don't we go to the place Tsuchi and I grew up this summer?

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.150
The place you and Tsuchi grew up?

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.750
I want to go!

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.190
We'll ask Hiiragi-chan and Koume-chan if they'd like to come, too.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:04.860
Really? What about Tsuchi?

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:05.790
Of course.

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.790
Hooray!

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:08.370
W-why me?

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.930
Oh, are you going on a trip together?

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.180
Yamamoto-sensei!

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:18.960
We're going to the place mommy and Tsuchi grew up over the summer.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.560
That sounds like fun.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.420
You should come too, Yamamoto-sensei.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:24.640
Me too?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.250
What are you saying, Anzu?

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.960
What a good idea.

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.330
Would you like to join us, Yamamoto-sensei?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.180
What? I wouldn't want to intrude.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.980
You wouldn't be. Right, Tsuchi?

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.780
Huh? Uh, right. You should come, too.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.290
Let's go together.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.840
We're going to ask Hii-chan and Koume-chan to come, too.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:46.630
Really? Perhaps I'll join you, then.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:50.910
I'm looking forward to traveling with you, Sakura-san, Tsuchida-sensei.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:51.760
Me, too.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:54.560
You too, Anzu-chan.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.250
Me, too.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.960
"A Hanamaru Summer Vacation"

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.350
Tsuchi, this is just like a honeymoon.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.720
Anzu, a honeymoon is a trip newlyweds take with just the two of them.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.520
But don't you think this would make a nice honeymoon?

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.480
Right, Yamamoto-sensei?

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:22.740
You're right. This is lively and fun.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.850
Y-you're right. A honeymoon with friends isn't bad at all.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:28.820
Really?

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.330
You're so positive today, Tsuchi.

00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:35.860
Tsuchi, you must be popular to have so many brides.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.160
Huh? What do you mean?

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:42.380
If we're on a honeymoon, that makes all of us his brides.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.230
What? You mean Yamamoto-sensei, too?

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:47.850
Really? Me, too?

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.170
Does that make me a bride, too?

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:53.220
Polygamy is prohibited by law.

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.090
I guess we're all marrying Tsuchida-sensei together.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:02.180
Fine, but I still love Tsuchi the most!

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.540
You playboy, Tsuchi!

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.530
W-what are you talking about, Senpai?

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.160
You playboy.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:11.830
Have the stars and planets aligned?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.250
Let's try to keep it down inside the train.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.280
You too, Anzu.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.500
But...

00:04:17.830 --> 00:04:22.010
I'm sorry, Tsuchida-sensei. Sorry, Anzu-chan.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.170
I took the joke too far.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.210
Oh no, I'm not bothered by it at all.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.320
Tsuchi, you haven't changed at all.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.420
What's that supposed to mean, senpai?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:35.530
What do you mean?

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:40.310
How do you know Tsuchida-sensei, Sakura-san?

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:44.720
Tsuchi was in love with me and always followed me around.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:45.990
What?

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:46.420
Is that so?

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:48.050
That's not true!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.280
What are you saying, senpai?

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.820
Sakura-senpai was a big shot always dragging me all over the place.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.780
Was that it?

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:02.980
Once we exit this tunnel, we'll be in Tsuchi and my hometown.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.390
There are so many sunflowers.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:15.340
So this is where Tsuchi grew up.

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.200
It's not so bad.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.940
There's a convenience store a short walk away.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.580
Yamamoto-sensei, I'll carry your bag.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.600
Huh? I can't let you do that.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:31.320
There's a slope up ahead, so I'd appreciate it if you'd look after the children.

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:33.400
Really? In that case...

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.400
You're so kind, Tsuchi.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:39.360
I know. I'll take your luggage, too.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:40.530
Thank you.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:49.730
It's been so long since my brother last came home.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:53.760
You must have had quite the trip coming out here.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.480
It's nice to see you again, ma'am.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.550
Oh, my.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.370
How cute!

00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:04.860
Nice to meet you, ma'am. I'm Anzu.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:05.990
I'm Hiiragi.

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:06.650
I'm Koume.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.290
Thanks, Tsuchi.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.580
I wouldn't be a preschool teacher if I gave up this easily.

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:17.320
I'm sorry for making you carry my luggage.

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:18.940
Not at all. This is nothing.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.270
Oh? Um...

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:25.620
Oh, nice to meet you. My name is Yamamoto.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.080
Oh, my!

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:29.590
Brother...

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.050
Hey, Satsuki.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.800
Another frog.

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:32.870
Hello, Satsuki-chan.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:34.300
This one's a toad.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.830
Oh, hello.

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.180
Sorry for barging in with so many.

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:41.960
It's fine. It's fun to have so many guests.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:43.680
Are your parents well?

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.080
They're still overseas, aren't they?

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:49.040
Yes. They're living peacefully over there.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.390
So, Anzu-chan is your child, Sakura-san.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.370
Yup.

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.860
I never thought you'd bring home a girl like her.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:06:59.920
What do you think of my boy?

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.730
He's always very kind to me.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.120
He even carried my luggage here.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.140
Oh, really?

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.390
What should we do about the betrothal money?

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.390
Hii-chan, what's betrothal money?

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:20.570
Betrothal money is the funds families traditionally exchange to affirm an engagement.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:22.230
What's an engagement?

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.720
A promise of marriage.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:25.350
Marriage?

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.190
W-what are you saying, mom?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.910
Yamamoto-sensei and I aren't involved like that!

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:32.110
What is it, then?

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:36.650
What would you call it, Yamamoto-sensei?

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.710
"Sensei?"

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:42.370
Oh, I forgot to mention I'm Tsuchida-sensei's colleague.

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.940
"Colleague?"

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:49.620
I came along to help look after the children.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.880
Thank you for your hospitality during my brief stay.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:58.150
I'm sorry. It looks like I caused some confusion.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.350
Not at all. I...

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:03.350
That's a shame. I thought I'd finally get to see some grandchildren.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.850
Tsuchi will exchange betrothal money with me!

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:10.900
You're going to be Naozumi's bride, Anzu?

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:14.020
Please allow me to call you "mother."

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:17.240
Huh? Is "Naozumi" Tsuchi?

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.820
This is how you write it in kanji.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:23.210
I see.

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.950
I'd better start calling Tsuchi "Naozumi-san."

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:31.990
Anzu-chan, you really like Tsuchida-sensei, don't you?

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.290
Yup.

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.930
You can keep calling me Tsuchi for now.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.340
I wonder what's wrong with my brother.

00:08:47.190 --> 00:08:48.840
Tsuchi seems down.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.750
Huh? Uh, yeah.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.010
Forget about him. He's at the height of his youth.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:56.070
His youth?

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:57.110
What do you mean?

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:58.860
Let's see...

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.510
I know.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.860
Why don't we go to the river tomorrow?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.490
The river?

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.300
I guess you could say it's a place that holds memories for us.

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:34.360
The cold water feels great.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.120
Why don't you swim too, Tsuchi?

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:38.400
I'm fine.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.220
Really?

00:09:40.970 --> 00:09:46.290
You know, ogling Yamamoto-sensei in her swimsuit isn't good for your health.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.130
What? Was it that obvious?

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:57.170
Senpai, why did you invite Yamamoto-sensei on this trip?

00:09:57.350 --> 00:10:01.460
"Why?" I'm just trying to give you a hand, Tsuchi.

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:06.230
I'm grateful for that, but won't Anzu be angry if she finds out?

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:09.450
Oh, right. I guess so.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.310
You mean you hadn't thought about it?

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.940
You're always so careless.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:15.900
It's not a big deal.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:17.800
Anyway...

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:20.760
We used to come here all the time.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.100
We'd always talk about stuff here.

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:25.750
Here...

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.910
What? You didn't go on the date?

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.500
Why not?

00:10:32.810 --> 00:10:35.400
You set me up without asking my opinion.

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:39.040
Huh? Didn't you say you like that girl?

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:41.250
This isn't what I wanted.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:45.630
Besides, a date isn't something you let other people set up for you.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:49.770
You'll never get a girlfriend with an attitude like that.

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:53.100
But I...

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.830
What about you, senpai? You don't have a boyfriend, do you?

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:59.250
I do. We started going out recently.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.550
It won't be long before we're lovers.

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:09.250
Your homeroom teacher?

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:12.830
He's just an old guy.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:13.870
What your mouth.

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:17.400
You just don't understand the appeal of an adult.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:19.290
But he's your teacher.

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.480
That'll never happen.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:28.750
I'll date him no matter what!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.350
I want to live for him.

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.320
You look like an idiot.

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:48.100
You'd better hurry up and find a girlfriend, Tsuchi.

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.320
Are you going to be a bachelor forever?

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:50.870
Oh, shut up.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:55.470
I wonder what they're talking about.

00:11:56.830 --> 00:12:02.360
Huh? Am I only on this trip with Yamamoto-sensei because of Sakura-senpai?

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:08.890
Sakura-senpai really did date and marry her teacher and became a mother...

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.630
...but I'm the same as I was back then.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.250
I guess nothing has changed.

00:12:16.610 --> 00:12:19.600
Isn't it nice that some places never change?

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.320
Nothing stays the same forever! I can change!

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:33.780
Brother!

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.670
Watch it, Tsuchi!

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:38.120
S-sorry!

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.710
Hey, brother.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.630
Oh, Satsuki. What's up?

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:53.480
The other day, I...

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:54.090
"Award"

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.480
Hey, Tsuchi!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:55.780
Come here!

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:58.930
Hiiragi-chan caught a big praying mantis.

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.310
I caught it.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:02.200
Sorry, I'll talk to you later.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:05.290
Yeah, there are big ones in this area.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.440
Oh, you.

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.360
"A Hanamaru Summer Festival"

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.750
Did you make all of this, Satsuki-chan?

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:16.240
This is spectacular.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:19.130
You make gnocchi.

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:25.290
Our club finished second in a statewide cooking contest with these.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.540
You're in a cooking club, huh?

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:35.600
Would you mind not telling my brother I made these until after he's eaten them?

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:39.530
I want to surprise him.

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:41.720
Okay.

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:42.890
Got it.

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:47.360
Let's eat!

00:13:55.520 --> 00:13:57.380
This is delicious.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:13:59.410
It's yummy!

00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:00.850
It really is.

00:14:00.880 --> 00:14:01.730
Yes.

00:14:02.080 --> 00:14:04.920
These chewy things are great.

00:14:05.660 --> 00:14:08.800
Yamamoto-sensei, I bet you made all of this.

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:12.010
No, I didn't make this.

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:15.590
Really? Was it you, mom?

00:14:16.010 --> 00:14:17.840
No, it wasn't me.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.960
Then it must have been Sakura-senpai.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:22.460
You must be a great wife.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:25.960
I could never make anything this complicated.

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.840
Think about it. There's a girl who's good at cooking here.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.750
Don't tell me it was the kids.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:32.760
Nope.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:33.550
It wasn't us.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:34.620
Wrong.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.700
Right, of course.

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:41.660
You're such an idiot!

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:45.070
I'm sorry, Satsuki...

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:48.250
...but there's no reason for you to get so angry.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.100
This is your fault, Tsuchi.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:54.340
Yeah, you're insensitive, Tsuchi.

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:59.220
Why didn't you just tell me you made it? Why'd you have to...

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:01.330
You're a jerk!

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:07.570
...and Tsuchi wouldn't stop looking at the girls in cute clothes.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:11.230
Anzu-chan, let's not tell that story.

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:12.330
Hey, Naozumi!

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.040
It's okay, Anzu-chan. Go ahead.

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:16.760
Okay.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:21.190
After that, Tsuchi read adult magazines in a convenience store.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:24.800
Anzu, I think you've got the wrong idea.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.270
You reap what you sow, Naozumi.

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:31.110
How pathetic.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:38.430
But Tsuchi saved me the time I couldn't climb back down a tree.

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:46.300
I fell out of the tree, but Tsuchi jumped in and protected me.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.220
I was so scared, I cried.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.960
You were great that one time.

00:15:51.370 --> 00:15:52.230
"One time," huh?

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:53.680
Is that so?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.700
Our Naozumi, huh?

00:15:55.860 --> 00:16:01.780
When he was holding me, I knew he was the one.

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:06.410
And the time I was attacked by a shark in the pool, Tsuchi...

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:07.780
Anzu, that didn't really happen.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.120
I was the shark.

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:12.220
I'm sorry.

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.340
Oh, I see.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:17.330
But he really did save Anzu when she fell out of the tree.

00:16:19.460 --> 00:16:22.060
He really is doing a proper job as a teacher.

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:23.510
That's right.

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:27.790
Even though I don't see it, he's working hard.

00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:30.610
But...

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:36.270
I never got the chance to show him.

00:16:44.240 --> 00:16:45.210
Anzu-chan...

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.640
I need to pee.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:49.580
Can you do it yourself?

00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:56.800
I'll be waiting right here. You don't need to rush.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:02.960
Anzu-chan, are you awake?

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.550
I'm awake.

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:09.740
Are you still mad at Tsuchi?

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:17.430
He's like that now, but he used to be different.

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:20.430
Really? What was he like?

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:22.670
Well, let's see...

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:25.410
He was a very kind brother.

00:17:26.090 --> 00:17:29.620
I always played with my brother.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:35.030
He always understood me even if I didn't say anything.

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.680
When I was worried about something, he'd notice right away.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.620
He's still like that.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:43.160
Really? You think so?

00:17:43.230 --> 00:17:45.450
Yeah. He's nice.

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:48.880
That's why everyone likes him.

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.820
It must be true if you think so.

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:55.160
But...

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:56.380
But...?

00:17:57.390 --> 00:18:00.870
Oh, that's right. There's a summer festival tomorrow.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:04.550
We can all go wearing <i>yukatas</i>.

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.600
There will be fireworks, too.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.650
Really? Fireworks?

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.210
What's everyone doing?

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.840
Everyone's paying their respects to the gods before the festival.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:23.150
I'll pay my respects, too.

00:18:23.150 --> 00:18:27.740
I'll pray for people to be more environmentally friendly.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:31.870
I wish for everyone to stay healthy.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:37.400
I also wish for my brother to come home more often.

00:18:43.770 --> 00:18:47.510
I wish to be man and wife with Tsuchi!

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.490
L-let's get out of here, Anzu.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.480
Hey, there's an <i>omikoshi</i> over there!

00:18:58.180 --> 00:19:00.630
Wait. We'll leave Anzu and the others behind.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.960
Hold hands, Koume and Hiiragi.

00:19:06.000 --> 00:19:06.750
Okay.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:07.390
Roger.

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:09.160
Hold me, Tsuchi!

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:15.440
You two can come with us.

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:19.070
You've been a big help on this trip, Yamamoto-sensei.

00:19:19.280 --> 00:19:21.000
You really have. Thank you.

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:24.780
It's no trouble at all. It's the least I can do.

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:26.780
I'm just happy to help.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.680
Satsuki, what are you doing over there? You'll get lost.

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:34.140
Hey!

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:49.630
Daddy...

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:50.730
Mommy...

00:19:52.390 --> 00:19:53.590
Brother...

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:55.640
Where are you?

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:57.920
Satsuki!

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:10.720
Brother!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.830
Sorry for leaving you by yourself.

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:18.220
I won't ever leave you again, so stop crying.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:23.360
They're selling your favorite <i>amazake</i> over there, so let's get some.

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:24.930
Okay.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.500
Those were the days.

00:20:34.680 --> 00:20:35.600
Satsuki!

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.600
Brother!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:44.510
How did you know I'd be here?

00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:46.750
I don't know.

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:53.560
Didn't I find you crying here when we were kids?

00:20:53.650 --> 00:20:55.900
I-I'm not crying!

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:57.140
I see.

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:03.690
Sorry about last night. The food you made was so delicious, I couldn't believe it.

00:21:03.850 --> 00:21:06.380
Really? It was that good?

00:21:06.640 --> 00:21:08.830
Yeah. I thought a professional chef had made it.

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:14.470
Our club won an award with that food.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:17.090
An award? That's amazing.

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:20.890
Isn't it? I even got a certificate. Do you want to see it later?

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:23.300
Really? I'd love to.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.140
Isn't this fun?

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:52.160
It certainly is.

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:54.570
Yeah.

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:57.270
<i>Tamaya</i>.

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:00.100
People first began saying "<i>tamaya</i>" in the Tokugawa Period...

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:31.580
Sakura here.

00:23:31.580 --> 00:23:34.470
Nothing beats going home. Everyone had fun.

00:23:34.470 --> 00:23:37.320
It seems like Tsuchi was in a bit of trouble, though.

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:39.530
Can you three handle the rest?

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.990
Let's do it.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.990
Roger.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.990
Okay.

00:23:40.990 --> 00:23:44.690
Next week's episode is about a fishmonger and the appearance of Anzu's rival. Don't miss it!

00:23:42.310 --> 00:23:43.530
"A Hanamaru Fishmonger"

00:23:43.530 --> 00:23:44.790
"A Hanamaru Rival"

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:49.540
"See you next week!"
